IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 5 -- Commencement of Acts (ss 15 to 17).
-- The rules that fix a day or a moment of commencement (ss 15A, 15B, 15C(1), 15D, 15DA) are in qld-interpretation-time.l4;
-- this module has the rest of the Part: what a reference to enactment or to commencement refers to, and powers used before commencement.

§ `Part 5 -- Commencement of Acts`

§§ `s 15 -- References to enactment etc. of Acts`

-- "a reference to the enactment of an Act or the passing of an Act is a reference to the fact of the Act's having received the royal assent."
-- A statement of what the reference is a reference to: it closes (JUST FALSE for an Act that has not received assent).
-- src:201 | In an Act, a reference to the enactment of an Act or the passing of an Act is a reference to the fact of the Act’s having received the royal assent.
@ref s 15 (src:201-201)
GIVEN `the Act has received the royal assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is enacted or passed (s 15)` IS
    JUST `the Act has received the royal assent`

§§ `s 15C -- Commencement of citation and commencement provisions`

DECLARE `What a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the Act concerned`
    `the commencement of the provision in which the reference is`
    `the commencement of the relevant provision of the Act concerned`

-- (2): (a) if the other provisions commence, or are required to commence, on a single day or at a single time, the commencement of the remaining provisions;
-- (b) if (a) does not apply and the reference is in a provision of the Act concerned, the commencement of the provision; (c) in any other case, the relevant provision.
-- src:208 | (2) A reference in an Act to the commencement of the Act, or another Act, (the Act concerned), is a reference to—
-- src:209 | (a) if the provisions of the Act concerned (other than those providing for its citation and commencement) commence, or are required to commence, on a single day or at a single time—the commencement of the remaining provisions; or
-- src:210 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply and the reference is in a provision of the Act concerned—the commencement of the provision; or
-- src:211 | (c) in any other case—the commencement of the relevant provision of the Act concerned.
@ref s 15C(2) (src:208-211)
GIVEN `the provisions of the Act concerned, other than those providing for its citation and commencement, commence or are required to commence on a single day or at a single time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in a provision of the Act concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to`
DECIDE `what a reference to the commencement of an Act is a reference to (s 15C(2))` IS
    IF `the provisions of the Act concerned, other than those providing for its citation and commencement, commence or are required to commence on a single day or at a single time`
    THEN `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the Act concerned`
    ELSE IF `the reference is in a provision of the Act concerned`
         THEN `the commencement of the provision in which the reference is`
         ELSE `the commencement of the relevant provision of the Act concerned`

-- (3): subsection (1) applies despite anything in the Act unless the Act expressly provides that it does not apply.
-- FORK once the Act expressly provides that s 15C(1) does not apply: NOTHING (this subsection no longer answers; the Act's own provision governs) || JUST FALSE
-- src:212 | (3) Subsection (1) applies to an Act despite anything in the Act unless the Act expressly provides that it does not apply.
@ref s 15C(3) (src:212-212)
GIVEN `the Act expressly provides that subsection (1) does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15C(1) applies to the Act despite anything in the Act (s 15C(3))` IS
    IF `the Act expressly provides that subsection (1) does not apply` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:213 | (4) A reference in this section to the provisions of an Act providing for its citation includes a reference to the Act’s long title.
@ref s 15C(4) (src:213-213)
GIVEN `the thing is the Act's long title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference in s 15C to the provisions providing for citation includes the long title (s 15C(4))` IS
    IF `the thing is the Act's long title` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 15D -- Commencement by proclamation etc.`

DECLARE `Way of fixing a day or time of commencement` IS ONE OF
    `a single day or time for the Act or the provisions`
    `different days or times for different provisions`
    `any other way`

-- src:215 | (1) If an Act or provisions of an Act is or are expressed to commence on a day to be fixed by proclamation or other instrument—
-- src:216 | (a) a single day or time may be fixed; or
-- src:217 | (b) different days or times may be fixed for different provisions.
@ref s 15D(1) (src:215-217)
GIVEN `the Act or provisions are expressed to commence on a day to be fixed by proclamation or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of fixing a day or time of commencement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the way of fixing is open to the proclamation or other instrument (s 15D(1))` IS
    IF NOT `the Act or provisions are expressed to commence on a day to be fixed by proclamation or other instrument`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER way
        WHEN `any other way` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:218 | (2) If the day or time fixed by a proclamation for the commencement of an Act or a provision of an Act happens before the day on which the proclamation is notified (the notification day)—
-- src:219 | (a) the proclamation is valid; but
@ref s 15D(2) (src:218-219)
GIVEN `the day or time fixed by the proclamation happens before the day on which the proclamation is notified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proclamation is valid though the day or time fixed happens before the notification day (s 15D(2)(a))` IS
    IF `the day or time fixed by the proclamation happens before the day on which the proclamation is notified` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 15DA -- definitions and the authority for the regulation`

-- (1): assent day means the date of assent of (a) if the postponed law is an Act, the Act; (b) if a provision of an Act, the Act that enacts the provision.
-- src:223 | assent day means the date of assent of—
-- src:224 | (a) if the postponed law is an Act—the Act; or
-- src:225 | (b) if the postponed law is a provision of an Act—the Act that enacts the provision.
@ref s 15DA(1), definition assent day (src:223-225)
GIVEN `the postponed law is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of assent of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the date of assent of the Act that enacts the provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the assent day (s 15DA(1))` IS
    IF `the postponed law is an Act` THEN `the date of assent of the Act` ELSE `the date of assent of the Act that enacts the provision`

-- src:226 | postponed law means an Act or provision of an Act that does not commence on the assent day because a provision of an Act postpones its commencement until a day fixed under an instrument.
@ref s 15DA(1), definition postponed law (src:226-226)
GIVEN `it is an Act or a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not commence on the assent day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of an Act postpones its commencement until a day fixed under an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is a postponed law (s 15DA(1), definition postponed law)` IS
    JUST (`it is an Act or a provision of an Act` AND `it does not commence on the assent day` AND `a provision of an Act postpones its commencement until a day fixed under an instrument`)

DECLARE `Act under which a regulation extending the period may be made` IS ONE OF
    `the Act that is the postponed law`
    `the Act of which the postponed law is a provision`
    `an Act that the postponed law amends`
    `any other Act`

-- src:229 | (4) The regulation mentioned in subsection (3) may be made under—
-- src:230 | (a) the Act that is the postponed law; or
-- src:231 | (b) the Act of which the postponed law is a provision; or
-- src:232 | (c) an Act that the postponed law amends;
-- src:233 | as if the Act mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) included a provision that had commenced and authorised the regulation to be made.
@ref s 15DA(4) (src:229-233)
GIVEN act IS A `Act under which a regulation extending the period may be made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulation extending the period may be made under the Act (s 15DA(4))` IS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `any other Act` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 15E -- Commencement of paragraphs etc. in amending Act`

-- src:242 | If an Act amends another Act and the amendment is in the form of—
-- src:243 | (a) a paragraph, or subparagraph, of a section or subsection of the amending Act; or
-- src:244 | (b) any other provision that is not self-contained;
-- src:245 | the amendment may be given a separate commencement.
@ref s 15E (src:242-245)
GIVEN `the amendment is in the form of a paragraph, or subparagraph, of a section or subsection of the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is in the form of any other provision that is not self-contained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amendment may be given a separate commencement (s 15E)` IS
    IF `the amendment is in the form of a paragraph, or subparagraph, of a section or subsection of the amending Act` OR `the amendment is in the form of any other provision that is not self-contained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 17 -- Exercise of powers between enactment and commencement`

-- (1): if an empowering provision that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, (a) confer a power (to make an appointment, a statutory instrument, or do any other thing)
-- or (b) amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power, then (c) the power may be exercised and (d) anything may be done to enable it or bring it into effect, before the empowering provision commences.
-- The period is fixed by the text ("before the empowering provision commences"); once the empowering provision has commenced the section does not answer: NOTHING.
-- src:248 | (1) If a provision of an Act (the empowering provision) that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced—
-- src:249 | (a) confer a power—
-- src:250 | (i) to make an appointment; or
-- src:251 | (ii) to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:252 | (iii) to do any other thing; or
-- src:253 | (b) amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power;
-- src:254 | then—
-- src:255 | (c) the power may be exercised; and
-- src:256 | (d) anything may be done for the purpose of—
-- src:257 | (i) enabling the exercise of the power; or
-- src:258 | (ii) bringing the appointment, instrument or other thing into effect;
-- src:259 | before the empowering provision commences.
@ref s 17(1) (src:248-259)
GIVEN `the empowering provision does not commence on its enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, confer a power to make an appointment, to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character, or to do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised before the empowering provision commences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power may be exercised (s 17(1)(c))` IS
    IF    `the empowering provision does not commence on its enactment`
       AND (   `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, confer a power to make an appointment, to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character, or to do any other thing`
            OR `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power`)
       AND `the power is exercised before the empowering provision commences`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:248 | (1) If a provision of an Act (the empowering provision) that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced—
-- src:249 | (a) confer a power—
-- src:250 | (i) to make an appointment; or
-- src:251 | (ii) to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character; or
-- src:252 | (iii) to do any other thing; or
-- src:253 | (b) amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power;
-- src:254 | then—
-- src:255 | (c) the power may be exercised; and
-- src:256 | (d) anything may be done for the purpose of—
-- src:257 | (i) enabling the exercise of the power; or
-- src:258 | (ii) bringing the appointment, instrument or other thing into effect;
-- src:259 | before the empowering provision commences.
@ref s 17(1) (src:248-259)
GIVEN `the empowering provision does not commence on its enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, confer a power to make an appointment, to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character, or to do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment, instrument or other thing into effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is done before the empowering provision commences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `anything may be done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power or bringing it into effect (s 17(1)(d))` IS
    IF    `the empowering provision does not commence on its enactment`
       AND (   `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, confer a power to make an appointment, to make a statutory instrument of a legislative or administrative character, or to do any other thing`
            OR `the empowering provision would, had it commenced, amend a provision of another Act so that the other Act would confer such a power`)
       AND `the thing is done for the purpose of enabling the exercise of the power, or of bringing the appointment, instrument or other thing into effect`
       AND `the thing is done before the empowering provision commences`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): the basic and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument, and a provision requiring the additional power is treated as made under (1).
-- src:260 | (2) If—
-- src:261 | (a) an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument (the basic instrument-making power); and
-- src:262 | (b) a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend the Act mentioned in paragraph (a) so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument (the additional instrument-making power);
-- src:263 | then—
-- src:264 | (c) the basic instrument-making power and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument; and
-- src:265 | (d) any provision of the instrument that required an exercise of the additional instrument-making power is to be treated as made under subsection (1).
@ref s 17(2) (src:260-265)
GIVEN `an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend that Act so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basic and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument (s 17(2)(c))` IS
    IF `an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument` AND `a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend that Act so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:260 | (2) If—
-- src:261 | (a) an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument (the basic instrument-making power); and
-- src:262 | (b) a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend the Act mentioned in paragraph (a) so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument (the additional instrument-making power);
-- src:263 | then—
-- src:264 | (c) the basic instrument-making power and the additional instrument-making power may be exercised by making a single instrument; and
-- src:265 | (d) any provision of the instrument that required an exercise of the additional instrument-making power is to be treated as made under subsection (1).
@ref s 17(2) (src:260-265)
GIVEN `an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend that Act so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of the instrument required an exercise of the additional instrument-making power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision of the instrument is treated as made under subsection (1) (s 17(2)(d))` IS
    IF `an Act that has commenced confers a power to make a statutory instrument` AND `a provision of an Act that does not commence on its enactment would, had it commenced, amend that Act so as to confer additional power to make a statutory instrument`
    THEN JUST `the provision of the instrument required an exercise of the additional instrument-making power`
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of thing done under s 17(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an appointment`
    `an instrument or provision of an instrument that is necessary for a purpose mentioned in s 17(3)`
    `an instrument or provision of an instrument that is not necessary for a purpose mentioned in s 17(3)`

-- (3) and (4): the day a thing done under (1) takes effect.  (3)(c): on the making of the instrument; (3)(d): the later time if expressed to take effect at a later time.
-- (4)(c): on the commencement of the relevant empowering provision; (4)(d): the later time if expressed.
-- "The later time" is read as a later day than the day the thing would otherwise take effect.
-- FORK a day expressed in the instrument that is not later than the day under (c): the (c) day applies (the word "later") || the expressed day applies
-- src:266 | (3) If an instrument, or a provision of an instrument, is made under subsection (1) that is necessary for the purpose of—
-- src:267 | (a) enabling the exercise of a power mentioned in subsection (1)(a); or
-- src:268 | (b) bringing an appointment, instrument or other thing made or done under such a power into effect;
-- src:269 | the instrument or provision takes effect—
-- src:270 | (c) on the making of the instrument; or
-- src:271 | (d) if the instrument or provision is expressed to take effect at a later time—the later time.
@ref s 17(3) (src:266-271)
GIVEN `the day the instrument or provision is made` IS A DATE
      `the day it is expressed to take effect, if it is expressed to take effect at a later time` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day an instrument or provision necessary under s 17(3) takes effect (s 17(3))` IS
    CONSIDER `the day it is expressed to take effect, if it is expressed to take effect at a later time`
    WHEN JUST later THEN IF later GREATER THAN `the day the instrument or provision is made` THEN later ELSE `the day the instrument or provision is made`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the instrument or provision is made`

-- src:272 | (4) If—
-- src:273 | (a) an appointment is made under subsection (1); or
-- src:274 | (b) an instrument, or provision of an instrument, made under subsection (1) is not necessary for a purpose mentioned in subsection (3);
-- src:275 | the appointment, instrument or provision takes effect—
-- src:276 | (c) on the commencement of the relevant empowering provision; or
-- src:277 | (d) if the appointment, instrument or provision is expressed to take effect at a later time—the later time.
@ref s 17(4) (src:272-277)
GIVEN `the day the relevant empowering provision commences` IS A DATE
      `the day it is expressed to take effect, if it is expressed to take effect at a later time` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day an appointment, or an instrument or provision not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect (s 17(4))` IS
    CONSIDER `the day it is expressed to take effect, if it is expressed to take effect at a later time`
    WHEN JUST later THEN IF later GREATER THAN `the day the relevant empowering provision commences` THEN later ELSE `the day the relevant empowering provision commences`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the relevant empowering provision commences`

-- src:278 | (5) Anything done under subsection (1) does not confer a right, or impose a liability, on a person before the relevant empowering provision commences.
@ref s 17(5) (src:278-278)
GIVEN `the thing was done under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the relevant empowering provision commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `anything done under s 17(1) confers a right or imposes a liability on a person on the day (s 17(5))` IS
    IF `the thing was done under subsection (1)` AND `the day in question` LESS THAN `the day the relevant empowering provision commences`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to` IS ONE OF
    `the empowering provision`
    `the provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) as amended by the empowering provision`

-- src:279 | (6) After the enactment of a provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) but before the provision’s commencement, this section applies as if the references in subsections (1) and (4) to the commencement of the empowering provision were references to the commencement of the provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) as amended by the empowering provision.
@ref s 17(6) (src:279-279)
GIVEN `a provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) has been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that provision has not yet commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to`
DECIDE `the provision whose commencement subsections (1) and (4) refer to (s 17(6))` IS
    IF `a provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) has been enacted` AND `that provision has not yet commenced`
    THEN `the provision mentioned in subsection (1)(b) as amended by the empowering provision`
    ELSE `the empowering provision`
